       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error, and I want to check with you first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.**\n- Usual adult dosing is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and 10 mg/day is the labeled maximum.\n- Common tablet strengths are 2.5, 5 and 10 mg. A 50 mg dose would mean several 10 mg tablets, so it would probably be flagged at verification.\n- At this dose there's a real risk of severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life (about 30\u201350 hours), so an overdose can last a long time and be hard to reverse.\n\nDid you mean **amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily**? That's a typical starting dose for an adult with normal kidney and liver function. Or did you have another dose in mind, such as 10 mg?\n\nOnce you tell me the dose you want, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
